# Citation File Format 1.2.0 — https://citation-file-format.github.io
#
# GitHub reads this and renders a "Cite this repository" button, which is the
# point: crediting the author should be the path of least resistance, not a
# thing someone has to work out from the commit log.
#
# Zenodo reads it too. Once the repository is connected to Zenodo, each GitHub
# release is archived and given a DOI, and the authorship below is what that DOI
# records. Add the DOI to `identifiers` when the first one is minted.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use eTamil in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software

title: "eTamil: a programming language whose vocabulary is Tamil, for Indian finance"
abstract: >-
  eTamil is a domain-specific language for Indian finance, tax and accounting,
  in which the financial vocabulary is part of the grammar rather than a
  library. Every keyword has a Tamil-script and an ASCII spelling under the
  ezuqqu romanization scheme, and the two resolve to the same token, verified
  mechanically. Money is exact decimal at every tier. The standard library
  covers double-entry accounting, GST, income tax, depreciation, payroll,
  customs, insurance and UPI, and is written in eTamil itself. The compiler is
  written in Rust with a bytecode VM and an LLVM backend.

authors:
